    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "protocol_version": 14,
   "reason": "Windows host support for the CLI and simulator. The SDK's host channel moves behind kobo_protocol::channel, which stays an AF_UNIX socket on Unix, and OS entropy behind kobo-abi, whose Unix arm reads /dev/urandom exactly as the SDK did before; directory and file flushes share kobo_protocol::durability with the same open-and-fsync behavior on Unix. Every platform difference is cfg-gated to Windows arms. The wire protocol, its version, and Unix build behavior are unchanged, so published Store apps are unaffected.",
